Hello all,

Well, I had a successful back-to-back moderately quick ascension
streak (of 2).  This time I thought I would see how fast I could
ascend a lawful Valkyrie.  I figured that I could be speedy given the
advantageous equipment that she started with but it was the end game
that dragged.

Tenaya the Warrior          St:18/79 Dx:17 Co:20 In:10 Wi:16 Ch:14
Lawful
Astral Plane $:170 HP:119(266) Pw:24(37) AC:-18 Xp:15/303028 T:25181


Beginning of the game was pretty easy with the starting equipment.  I
finished with Minetown at around 15,000 turns and had already gotten
an amulet of reflection from Sokoban.  I was aided immensely by
BillDaCat's ghost with a magic whistle, a cloak of magic resistance, a
ring of teleport control, and a wand of enlightenment with which to id
my rings at the Oracle level.  Another stroke of good fortune was
finding a chameleon corpse and when my dog ate it, he turned into
a ...

[I love the anticipation!!!]

baluchitherium!  That cleared out Minetown and netted me 5 points of
protection.

I asended with Excalibur and a silver saber.  I also had Grayswandir
but I couldn't be bothered to enchant it up so I just kept it in my
bag.  Good thing that I did, because while waiting for Asmodeus at the
Sanctum I had both my weapons whipped out of my hands by horned or
barbed devils (or maybe it was a pit fiend).  Mojo was left on the
altar in Minetown.  Incidentally, I never found a cooperative white
unicorn and only managed to throw 1 named gem to one.  The rest of my
luck was from altar sacrifices.

Had one close call: an owlbear grabbed me while my wand of fire was in
my bag of holding and I thought, "I'm #twoweaponing, no problem!".
Well I got into the red life zone, despite a successful prayer.  That
was a learning experience.  Those owlbears and carnivorous apes can
surprise ya!

The end of the game was painfully tedious and even started to make me
(vaguely) nervous partly due to lack of loot and partly due to my own
haste:
Before the endgame I had only found 1 wand of teleportation and 1 wand
of death.  the death stick was used liberally on Rodney but it ran out
when he Double Troubled so I had to zap a hole in the floor, melee the
single Rodney that fell through with me and then recharge my death
wand.  Also, I only found 2 potions of paralysis but no ring of free
action.  I hit the wizard with a thrown potion on the Plane of Earth
and fortunately I woke up before he did and before the minotaur killed
me.  Fortunately I had plenty of blank blessed scrolls because I used
10 teleport zaps on the plane of air.  The Astral plane was mainly
meleed and jumped and in the summoning storms a couple of cockatrice
corpses were lying around; fortunately I got to them first and stoned
the angels and adventurers.

My wishes (0:2) were:
~ 2 blessed scrolls of charging (only got 1)
~ +2 grey dragon scale mail (rec'd +0; gray castle dragon left no
scales despite 6 undead turning zaps)
~ magic marker (midgame)
~ magic marker (so that I could recharge my wand of death/teleport)
~ blessed ring of conflict (air was still challenging, though)
~ blessed ring of levitation (for the Planes)

Once I finished the Quest on Level 11, I levelported to the Castle,
cleared it and the Valley and then used Asmodeus to map Gehennom.  I
didn't realize just how meagre a level 15 valkyrie's power is (37 in
my case) !  I could not even do 2 self-teleports, so I had to #jump my
last 5000 turns.  Fortunately ^a works also but it is a whole lot of
keystrokes.  Because I couldn't teleport my way through the levels and
even had to explore the main dungeon (all from 11 to 26, ack) Rodney
visited me quite often.  I had to do more fighting on the ascension
run than while mapping Gehennom or even on the quest.  Fortunately I
remembered to blindfold while climbing because I didn't visit Medusa's
level until the Ascension run.

Oh yeah, despite having a stack of 7 elven daggers I never enchanted
them (not enough scrolls or marker charges for even my off-hand +2
silver saber) nor did I ever exercise my skill in dagger throwing.  I
just hacked my way through partly because I'm too lazy to pick the
daggers back up.  Shuriken were plentiful so I just used those.

I had dreams of acquiring 18/** strength from giant corpses but
despite wearing a ring of regeneration and hunger, jumping to and
fro,  and casting as much as my measly Pw37 could handle, it just took
forever to get below satiated so I just let it be.



